  "name": null,
  "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h}).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h})\\,=\\,\\,$ | ${e}^{x}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $8{sin}^{2}\u2061(x)$ |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x).$\n\nWe apply the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h}) & =\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot h(x)-f(x)\\cdot {h}^{\u2032}(x)}{[h(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})}^{\u2032}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x))-(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x))^{\u2032}}{(-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x))-(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x))}{16{sin}^{2}\u2061(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x))}{16{sin}^{2}\u2061(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x))}{8{sin}^{2}\u2061(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
